1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,128
Buster Gallon, the Betrayer

2
00:00:08,124 --> 00:00:11,176
That Buffalo Crush!

3
00:00:11,176 --> 00:00:14,499
He told us to leave it to him, and look what happens!

4
00:00:14,499 --> 00:00:17,827
He gets sealed and that's the end of it!

5
00:00:17,827 --> 00:00:20,768
Aren't you over reacting? After all, you just sat by and watched it happen.

6
00:00:20,768 --> 00:00:21,695
Quiet!

7
00:00:21,695 --> 00:00:26,297
I suppose... it's really sad to lose a member of our crew.

8
00:00:26,297 --> 00:00:33,682
We were going to rule the world with the Metal Breath in our hands.

9
00:00:33,682 --> 00:00:36,109
B-Buster... Gallon... what do you think you're doing?!

10
00:00:36,109 --> 00:00:37,901
Oh, shall I explain?

11
00:00:37,901 --> 00:00:44,109
This is an invention I completed today that can temporarily suspend all function of a Metal Cardbot.

12
00:00:44,109 --> 00:00:47,139
With this, I can take the Metal Breath all for myself.

13
00:00:47,139 --> 00:00:49,640
You son of a... You dare betray me?!

14
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:51,823
Wouldn't you say that's more like a pirate?

15
00:00:51,823 --> 00:00:53,591
Farewell... Captain.

16
00:00:56,338 --> 00:00:58,731
Buster Gallon!!

17
00:01:09,852 --> 00:01:12,730
Could you put that down here?

18
00:01:12,730 --> 00:01:14,373
What are you guys making?

19
00:01:14,373 --> 00:01:15,229
A shelter!

20
00:01:15,229 --> 00:01:17,875
A shelter? You mean something like a bunker?

21
00:01:17,875 --> 00:01:22,450
Captain Black Hook's rule. Never lose treasure he set his eye on!

22
00:01:22,450 --> 00:01:26,906
Need to build up defenses to keep planet Machina's treasure safe!

23
00:01:26,906 --> 00:01:29,426
But don't you think there's been a misunderstanding?

24
00:01:29,426 --> 00:01:32,658
A Metal Cardbot can't use the Metal Breath by themselves.

25
00:01:32,658 --> 00:01:33,531
That's right.

26
00:01:33,531 --> 00:01:39,150
If we could use the Metal Breath, I would have sealed the Cardbots myself.

27
00:01:39,150 --> 00:01:41,917
So... you mean, even if Black Hook takes the Metal Breath...

28
00:01:41,917 --> 00:01:45,617
...he couldn't possibly make a Metal Cardbot army?

29
00:01:45,617 --> 00:01:49,971
Wouldn't explaining all of this to Black Hook make him give up?

30
00:01:49,971 --> 00:01:52,257
Listen. That bad idea.

31
00:01:52,257 --> 00:01:53,271
Why's that?

32
00:01:53,271 --> 00:01:56,944
Us three tried really hard to steal Metal Breath.

33
00:01:56,944 --> 00:02:01,349
If he learn he cannot use it, he use all his might to destroy it instead.

34
00:02:01,349 --> 00:02:02,733
We can't let that happen!

35
00:02:02,733 --> 00:02:05,079
Then why don't we make the first move?

36
00:02:05,079 --> 00:02:10,360
Yeah, you said it! They say a good offense is the best defense!

37
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:11,997
Hey, Buffalo Crush!

38
00:02:11,997 --> 00:02:13,259
Huh? What?

39
00:02:13,259 --> 00:02:16,431
You know where Black Hook's hideout is.

40
00:02:16,431 --> 00:02:18,795
Tell us where we can find it!

41
00:02:18,795 --> 00:02:22,258
Yeah, tell us! Tell us, Buffalo Crush!

42
00:02:22,358 --> 00:02:24,853
Me can't tell you!

43
00:02:27,376 --> 00:02:28,703
Where are you going?!

44
00:02:28,703 --> 00:02:30,215
Blue Cop, let's go follow him!

45
00:02:30,215 --> 00:02:30,896
Alright.

46
00:02:32,408 --> 00:02:32,884
Jun!

47
00:02:33,110 --> 00:02:34,103
Mom.

48
00:02:34,387 --> 00:02:35,424
Hello, everyone.

49
00:02:35,424 --> 00:02:36,359
Uh... Hello.

50
00:02:37,495 --> 00:02:39,194
What are you doing here?

51
00:02:39,545 --> 00:02:42,593
The car that just left, wasn't that our Buffy?

52
00:02:42,593 --> 00:02:45,152
Our Buffy? You mean Buffalo Crush?

53
00:02:45,152 --> 00:02:47,579
Yes. I have something for him.

54
00:02:47,579 --> 00:02:48,706
Can you deliver it for me?

55
00:02:48,706 --> 00:02:50,572
For him? What is it?

56
00:02:50,572 --> 00:02:53,328
It's just a little gift I made for him myself.

57
00:02:59,896 --> 00:03:02,168
What are you doing all the way out here, Buffalo Crush?

58
00:03:02,168 --> 00:03:03,424
Jun...

59
00:03:03,424 --> 00:03:06,651
Here. My mom made something special for you.

60
00:03:06,651 --> 00:03:07,912
It's a doll she knitted herself!

61
00:03:07,912 --> 00:03:10,521
Thank you... but I can't.

62
00:03:10,521 --> 00:03:11,551
What do you mean?

63
00:03:11,551 --> 00:03:14,997
Black Hook is first friend I made before coming to Earth.

64
00:03:14,997 --> 00:03:17,370
Me won't betray him.

65
00:03:17,370 --> 00:03:19,752
We aren't asking you to do anything.

66
00:03:19,752 --> 00:03:22,858
My Mom poured her heart into this doll she made for you.

67
00:03:22,858 --> 00:03:24,520
So I really hope you'll accept it!

68
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:27,750
Yuri's heart?

69
00:03:28,408 --> 00:03:31,204
Transform into a car! I'll put it on for you!

70
00:03:35,674 --> 00:03:36,812
It look good?

71
00:03:36,812 --> 00:03:39,840
Yeah! It looks great on you!

72
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,978
Huh? What's going on?

73
00:03:41,978 --> 00:03:43,706
There's been an explosion at a warehouse in the port area.

74
00:03:43,706 --> 00:03:44,804
It's on the news right now.

75
00:03:44,804 --> 00:03:45,853
What?

76
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:48,948
-but the warehouse hasn't been used in a while.
-Is this it?

77
00:03:48,948 --> 00:03:52,949
-and there hasn't been anyone seen in the vicinity. The police...
-That...

78
00:03:52,949 --> 00:03:54,384
Our hideout!

79
00:03:54,384 --> 00:03:56,878
Really? Is it close to here?

80
00:03:56,878 --> 00:03:59,099
-Something bad happened to Captain!
-Hey!

81
00:03:59,299 --> 00:04:01,848
Don't leave me behind again!

82
00:04:02,954 --> 00:04:05,801
Blue Cop! The warehouse that blew up was Black Hook's Hideout!

83
00:04:05,801 --> 00:04:06,723
What?

84
00:04:06,723 --> 00:04:08,912
I'm headed there now. Meet me there!

85
00:04:09,562 --> 00:04:10,924
Everyone. Let's head out!

86
00:04:10,924 --> 00:04:11,560
Right!

87
00:04:26,127 --> 00:04:27,956
S-s-stop!

88
00:04:31,692 --> 00:04:33,310
Where are you, Captain?!

89
00:04:35,653 --> 00:04:37,100
Hey, hey, look!

90
00:04:37,187 --> 00:04:39,006
Could it be?...

91
00:04:39,006 --> 00:04:41,126
It must be one of the robots from the rumors! Camera, now!

92
00:04:41,126 --> 00:04:42,022
Already on it!

93
00:04:42,622 --> 00:04:45,394
Jun. I will be arriving soon with Shadow X.

94
00:04:45,394 --> 00:04:48,519
Alright. We have to chase that helicopter out of here!

95
00:04:48,519 --> 00:04:49,451
Leave it to me!

96
00:04:53,338 --> 00:04:54,262
Watch out!

97
00:04:54,262 --> 00:04:55,629
Coming through!

98
00:04:55,629 --> 00:04:57,595
Hey, watch where you're flying!

99
00:04:58,403 --> 00:05:01,172
It's dangerous here. Please keep your distance.

100
00:05:05,836 --> 00:05:07,500
Jun! All clear up here!

101
00:05:10,362 --> 00:05:11,596
Huh?!

102
00:05:12,894 --> 00:05:14,802
Aah!

103
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:19,877
Come back, both of you!

104
00:05:21,831 --> 00:05:22,776
Are you okay?

105
00:05:22,776 --> 00:05:24,177
My engine has been hit.

106
00:05:24,177 --> 00:05:25,901
...my propeller...

107
00:05:27,670 --> 00:05:30,415
To think you'd bring the Metal Breath right to me.

108
00:05:30,415 --> 00:05:32,362
That makes things easier.

109
00:05:32,362 --> 00:05:35,925
What happen here Buster Gallon? Where our Captain?!

110
00:05:35,925 --> 00:05:41,401
It seemed to me that it would take much too long to get our hands on the Metal Breath with him in the way.

111
00:05:41,401 --> 00:05:42,865
So I removed him from the equation.

112
00:05:42,865 --> 00:05:44,132
What?!

113
00:05:44,132 --> 00:05:46,199
And now, it's your turn!

114
00:05:49,545 --> 00:05:50,737
Buffalo Crush!

115
00:05:50,737 --> 00:05:52,956
Me... can't... move...

116
00:05:54,413 --> 00:05:56,180
Jun! Are you alright?

117
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:57,480
Is that?...

118
00:05:58,800 --> 00:05:59,675
Stay away!

119
00:05:59,675 --> 00:06:01,112
Buster Gallon!

120
00:06:01,112 --> 00:06:02,997
Ah. I have more customers.

121
00:06:06,766 --> 00:06:07,603
What's going on here?!

122
00:06:07,603 --> 00:06:09,237
Do I want to know?

123
00:06:09,649 --> 00:06:12,701
Just stand back and watch!

124
00:06:12,701 --> 00:06:14,379
Mega Trucker, setup!

125
00:06:14,379 --> 00:06:16,610
Mega Power Shield!

126
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:18,144
Twin Vulcan!

127
00:06:20,487 --> 00:06:23,625
Mega Ambler! Please find out what happened to Blue Cop!

128
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,297
A powerful magnetic field is blocking all movement of Metal Cardbots.

129
00:06:30,427 --> 00:06:32,754
Found it! The magnetic field is coming from underground!

130
00:06:34,511 --> 00:06:37,528
If you value your friends' lives, then hand over the Metal Breath!

131
00:06:37,528 --> 00:06:38,848
It's a bomb!

132
00:06:38,848 --> 00:06:41,278
Everyone, come back!

133
00:06:41,278 --> 00:06:42,331
Huh?! Why isn't it working?

134
00:06:42,331 --> 00:06:46,840
It's no use. When caught in my magnetic field, all of your functions become inactive.

135
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:48,396
This guy's good.

136
00:06:48,396 --> 00:06:49,918
He really did his homework.

137
00:06:49,918 --> 00:06:54,766
Of course. Black Hook knew nothing of the Metal Breath besides that it was a treasure of planet Machina.

138
00:06:54,766 --> 00:06:55,925
But I'm different!

139
00:06:55,925 --> 00:07:00,379
That object is nothing more than a system constructed by the mother computer, Deus Machina.

140
00:07:00,379 --> 00:07:05,805
Even if it's locked to prevent Metal Cardbots from using it, there's always a way to crack the code if you put in the time.

141
00:07:05,805 --> 00:07:08,331
Now. Hand over the Metal Breath!

142
00:07:08,331 --> 00:07:11,350
For I, Buster Gallon, will gather the Metal Cardbots around the universe

143
00:07:11,350 --> 00:07:14,483
and construct an empire across the galaxy!

144
00:07:14,483 --> 00:07:17,490
Y-you're out of your mind, Buster Gallon...

145
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:18,874
I'll tell you three important things!

146
00:07:19,528 --> 00:07:21,213
Are you talking to me?

147
00:07:21,213 --> 00:07:22,680
What could you possibly have to say?

148
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:23,470
One!

149
00:07:23,470 --> 00:07:26,742
In my experience, a talkative villain always lets down his guard and loses!

150
00:07:26,742 --> 00:07:31,122
What do you mean, let down my guard?! Your fate is in my hands!

151
00:07:31,122 --> 00:07:34,370
Two! I still have eight friends left in my team!

152
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:37,908
Eight? Huh. There were two taken back just now...

153
00:07:37,908 --> 00:07:39,475
One is missing!

154
00:07:41,516 --> 00:07:43,814
I found the magnetic field emitting device!

155
00:07:43,814 --> 00:07:45,129
This can't be!

156
00:07:45,129 --> 00:07:46,720
When did you?...

157
00:07:47,737 --> 00:07:48,706
I'm free!

158
00:07:49,637 --> 00:07:51,338
And three!

159
00:07:51,338 --> 00:07:53,225
Our hearts are connected with Jun's!

160
00:07:53,225 --> 00:07:54,600
Even without orders-

161
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,286
-We know what we need to do.

162
00:07:57,773 --> 00:07:59,444
Then just try and stop me!

163
00:07:59,444 --> 00:08:00,444
We won't let you win!

164
00:08:01,151 --> 00:08:02,468
Phoenix Fire, setup!

165
00:08:11,514 --> 00:08:12,677
Strike!

166
00:08:12,875 --> 00:08:15,620
Then how about this?!

167
00:08:16,134 --> 00:08:17,720
Wild Guardy, setup!

168
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:24,848
What is this?!

169
00:08:26,574 --> 00:08:27,379
Jun!

170
00:08:31,612 --> 00:08:32,808
Guys!

171
00:08:32,808 --> 00:08:35,903
That's another invention of mine, the freeze grenade.

172
00:08:35,903 --> 00:08:39,571
A genius like me always has a plan B!

173
00:08:39,571 --> 00:08:42,423
Now... about that Metal Breath.

174
00:08:42,423 --> 00:08:45,267
Hold... on...!

175
00:08:45,267 --> 00:08:49,432
Oh, Buffalo Crush... you should really learn when to give up.

176
00:08:49,432 --> 00:08:53,745
Me have... warmth of human's heart inside me.

177
00:08:53,745 --> 00:08:57,750
As long as that love remain, the flames of my engine will never...

178
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:59,806
...go out!

179
00:09:02,942 --> 00:09:04,811
Alright! It's our turn now!

180
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,456
Metal Breath, pickup!

181
00:09:08,350 --> 00:09:09,754
Buffalo Crush, setup!

182
00:09:19,552 --> 00:09:21,417
Buffalo Vision!

183
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:25,100
Buffalo... Vision!

184
00:09:26,873 --> 00:09:29,692
Let's get him! Buffalo Moonsault!

185
00:09:32,134 --> 00:09:34,918
Buffalo...

186
00:09:34,918 --> 00:09:37,379
Moonsault!

188
00:09:38,182 --> 00:09:40,248
Buster Blaster!

189
00:09:54,889 --> 00:09:58,139
Metal Cardbot, change up!

190
00:10:17,176 --> 00:10:19,427
Buster Gallon, sealed!

191
00:10:20,793 --> 00:10:23,658
You're another one of our friends, now!

192
00:10:26,182 --> 00:10:27,681
Finally.

193
00:10:27,681 --> 00:10:30,490
I'm so sick of being unable to move!

194
00:10:30,490 --> 00:10:33,000
Looks like the freeze grenade didn't last too long.

195
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,192
That's good!

196
00:10:34,192 --> 00:10:35,672
You did it, Jun.

197
00:10:35,672 --> 00:10:38,379
Not just me, it was all thanks to Buffalo Crush!

198
00:10:38,379 --> 00:10:39,873
You did a great job.

199
00:10:39,873 --> 00:10:41,340
You saved us all.

200
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:42,250
Thank you.

201
00:10:42,250 --> 00:10:45,363
We won... but where Captain?

202
00:10:46,384 --> 00:10:47,187
What's that?!

203
00:10:47,187 --> 00:10:47,975
Is it an earthquake?!

204
00:10:54,264 --> 00:10:55,822
B-Black Hook!

205
00:10:56,023 --> 00:10:56,331
You're alive.

206
00:10:57,368 --> 00:11:00,610
Buster Gallon's puny little bomb isn't enough to stop me!

207
00:11:00,610 --> 00:11:02,504
Captain!

208
00:11:02,504 --> 00:11:06,240
Buffalo Crush. You're still calling me Captain?!

209
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,657
Uh-huh!

210
00:11:07,657 --> 00:11:08,802
You fool!

211
00:11:10,589 --> 00:11:12,475
That's going too far.

212
00:11:12,787 --> 00:11:14,359
And you, Earthling child!

213
00:11:14,359 --> 00:11:17,702
I will take that Metal Breath from you one day, so you'd better be prepared!

215
00:11:17,902 --> 00:11:21,287
A pirate never goes back on his word!

216
00:11:21,287 --> 00:11:24,321
We'll never let you get your way! You hear that?!

217
00:11:25,735 --> 00:11:27,451
The Captain hit me...

